Technology, Network Engineering & Project Development Trustee

SKYWAVE RURALNET SCIO is seeking an enthusiastic and technically experienced volunteer trustee to help shape our rural digital inclusion programme.

About SKYWAVE

SKYWAVE works to reduce digital exclusion in rural and underserved communities through:

Digital connectivity;
Provision of digital devices;
Digital skills training; and
Ongoing digital support.

We are developing pilot projects in IV26, IV27 and IV28, building on our broadband research and further community needs assessment.

The Role

The Technology, Network Engineering & Project Development Trustee will provide technical expertise, strategic advice and governance oversight to help SKYWAVE develop a practical and sustainable delivery model.

Key Activities
Advise the Board on network and technology strategy;
Provide technical input into rural connectivity and digital inclusion projects;
Review technical feasibility, risks and proposed solutions;
Advise on network architecture, equipment and technical standards;
Contribute to pilot planning and project development;
Provide appropriate oversight of external technical contractors; and
Help ensure SKYWAVE's technology model is scalable, secure and sustainable.
Skills We Are Looking For

Experience or knowledge in one or more of:

Network engineering;
Wireless networking;
Telecommunications;
IT infrastructure or systems;
Cybersecurity;
Technical project management;
Network architecture; or
Technology procurement.

Experience in rural connectivity or digital inclusion is desirable but not essential.

What We Offer

This is an unpaid volunteer trustee role offering an opportunity to use your technical expertise for public benefit and help shape a new rural digital inclusion charity from its development and pilot stage.

The role is primarily strategic and governance-focused. Physical network installation and specialist technical delivery will be undertaken by appropriately qualified contractors and partners.

How to Apply

Please send a CV or short skills profile and a brief statement explaining your interest and what you could contribute to skywaveruralnet@gmail.com

Shortlisted candidates will have a brief informal discussion with SKYWAVE.

**Job Overview**  
Direct, oversee and manage complex labeling and regulatory projects, ensuring quality deliverables on time and within budget. Ensure that all project work is completed in accordance with standard operating procedures, policies and practices.

**Essential Functions**  
• May act as a Project Manager for a large stand-alone program, involving several regulatory or technical deliverables and/or region, and/or operation; Undertakes risk analysis, management and contingency plans, as appropriate;  
• Provides strategic regulatory and/or technical consultancy on a variety of projects, internally and externally, using innovative solutions where appropriate;  
• May manage meetings with Regulatory Agencies;  
• May write and/or review a complete single service regulatory proposal and defend costs and timelines to clients;  
• Provides mentorship to junior colleagues and advise others on many regulatory document types;  
• May plan and deliver workshops or presentations on Labeling / Regulatory Affairs topics for conferences or publications;  
• May be assigned as Reviewer and/or Approver for Regulatory standard operating procedures or cross-functional standard operating procedures owned by other operations;  
• May support global regulatory or technical initiatives or act as a Subject Matter Expert.   
• Performs other tasks or assignments, as delegated by Regulatory management;

**Qualifications**  
• Bachelor's Degree Degree in LiveScience or related discipline Req Or  
• Master's Degree Degree in Life science or related discipline  
• At least 12 years relevant experience including 8 years labeling regulatory experience or combination of education, training and experience  
• Extensive experience in EU labeling updates submissions  
• Advanced negotiating and influencing skills and the ability to identify and resolve issues, using flexible adaptable approach. Remains calm, assertive and diplomatic in challenging interactions with customers  
• Strong software and computer skills, including MS Office applications  
• Acts as a role model to junior colleagues; possesses a positive attitude and communication style to customers and colleagues. Communicates effectively with all levels of the organization and remains motivated and enthusiastic in times of change and other pressure situations  
• Ability to exercise independent judgement taking calculated risks when making decisions  
• Applicable certifications and licenses as required by country, state, and/or other regulatory bodies

Join Kroll's Global Investigations, Diligence and Compliance Core team and gain hands-on experience in the dynamic field of compliance consulting. We are seeking motivated and detail-oriented individuals to contribute as new joiners here at Kroll.

Through a combination of expertise, global research capabilities and flexible technology tools, the Investigations, Diligence and Compliance Core practice of Kroll helps clients take a risk-based approach toward meeting obligations or remediating failures regarding anti-bribery, anti-corruption and related regulatory mandates. These include pre-transactional intelligence; vendor, supplier and distributor due diligence; vendor screening and monitoring; country/industry risk; and bespoke inquiries.

At Kroll, your work will help deliver clarity to our clients’ most complex governance, risk, and transparency challenges. Apply now to join One team, One Kroll.

**RESPONSIBILITIES:**

Have an analytical mind and a passion for research and investigation? Come join our thriving global team and work with Fortune 500 clients in a highly collaborative, fast-paced environment!

We are committed to the continuous professional development of our people; hone your skills and master new ones with the support of a world-class in-house training program. Become a regional specialist, learn to lead, deepen your linguistic abilities, build technical expertise—the opportunities are endless.

We currently have opportunities for researchers in multiple offices across the world. The right candidate will have outstanding English-language reading and writing skills, meticulous attention to detail, a sense of curiosity, the ability to learn quickly, and a dedication to client satisfaction. Fluency in other languages is highly desired.

* Conduct increasingly complex English- and foreign-language research using public record databases, commercial and proprietary databases, media sources and the Internet.
* Analyze and synthesize relevant research findings.
* Write well-structured, concise, logical and objective reports to provide clients with an accurate assessment of the findings. Most reports are written in English.
* Manage multiple assignments from start to finish, conducting extensive Internet, database, and media research into companies and individuals to provide our clients with an accurate assessment of the status legitimacy, general background, and overall reputation of a subject company and its principals.

**REQUIREMENTS:**

* Native or equivalent English language proficiency in reading comprehension
* Extremely strong reading and writing skills in English, ability to quickly and effectively summaries information from multiple sources into a concise analytical assessment;
* Proficiency in either Arabic, Dutch, French, German, Italian, Russian, or Turkish is required.
* 1-2 years of professional experience (including internships)
* Undergraduate or graduate degree at an accredited university majoring in: International Relations/Affairs, Regional Studies, Political Science, Criminal Justice, Law or other related areas of study;
* Ability to conduct online research using various primary and secondary sources;
* Ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment;
* Ability to accept and apply constructive feedback;
* Ability to manage and prioritize several projects or assignments simultaneously while meeting tight deadlines;
* Customer-service orientation with a dedication to quality and a strong attention to detail.

**PREFERRED SKILLS**

* Organizational and time management competencies;
* Attention to detail;
* Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing;
* Intellectually curious and adept at navigating ambiguity;
* Interest and understanding of current events, international affairs, financial regulations, and economics and/or finance;
* Detailed knowledge and understanding of current events, international affairs, economics and social risk issues;
* Basic knowledge of litigation, regulatory, sanctions and corporate organization / structure terminology and concepts;
* Experience working with diverse teams or in international environments is highly desirable;

**ABOUT KROLL**

Join the global leader in risk and financial advisory solutions—Kroll. With a nearly century-long legacy, we blend trusted expertise with cutting-edge technology to navigate and redefine industry complexities. As a part of One Team, One Kroll, you'll contribute to a collaborative and empowering environment, propelling your career to new heights. Ready to build, protect, restore and maximize our clients’ value? Your journey begins with Kroll.

In order to be considered for a position at Kroll, you must formally apply via careers.kroll.com. Please attach or upload a copy of your resume/CV in English for consideration.

*Kroll is committed to equal opportunity and diversity, and recruits people based on merit.*

# Technisch Project Manager (Avonmouth, UK)

* + Bristol, Verenigd Koninkrijk
* Projects

Hou je van een open cultuur, korte lijnen en een no-nonsense mentaliteit? Dan ben jij misschien wel dé collega, die we zoeken om ons dynamisch team te versterken. SEA-Tank Terminal, is een sterk groeiend tankopslagbedrijf in een internationale omgeving en is o.a. actief in de haven van Gent & Antwerpen. Wij zijn gespecialiseerd in de opslag van liquide goederen en logistieke afhandeling voor derden.

Voor een nieuw strategisch project in Avonmouth, in samenwerking met onze partner, zijn wij op zoek naar een **ervaren Technisch Project Manager**.

Het project omvat de ombouw van een LNG-installatie (Liquefied Natural Gas) naar LPG (propaan), inclusief de opzet van het toekomstig operationeel beheer van het tankpark. Het betreft een meerjarig traject (± 2 jaar) met aansluitend ondersteuning van het lokale operationele team om een vlotte en duurzame overdracht te garanderen.

#### **Jouw functie**

Als Technisch Project Manager ben je verantwoordelijk voor de overkoepelende opvolging en bewaking van het project. Je fungeert als senior sparringpartner voor het lokale projectteam en rapporteert rechtstreeks aan de directie van SEA-Tank.

Takenpakket:

* Je bewaakt de globale voortgang, planning, budget en mijlpalen;
* Je zorgt voor een sterke sense of urgency binnen het project;
* Je daagt het lokale team uit op kwaliteit, efficiëntie en respecteren van deadlines;
* Je werkt nauw samen met de lokale projectmanager;
* Je rapporteert periodiek aan de directie over voortgang, risico’s en beslissingspunten
* Je begeleidt het project van detailed engineering, over de bouwfase, tot oplevering en de eerste weken van operaties;
* Na oplevering ondersteun je het lokale operationele team om een vlotte transitie te verzekeren.

Je focus zal dus niet liggen op de dagelijkse operationele aansturing.

Je werkt vanuit Avonmouth, met sporadische verplaatsingen naar het projectteam in Antwerpen en het studiebureau in Spanje.

#### **Jouw profiel**

**Opleiding & achtergrond**

* Master in Ingenieurswetenschappen (Bouwkunde, Proces-chemie of Elektromechanica);

**Technische en projectervaring**

* Gedegen ervaring in technische projectomgevingen binnen Europa. Ervaring in het Verenigd Koninkrijk is een sterke troef.
* Ervaring met liquide bulk en/of gassen (LPG, LNG ...);

* Ervaring in tankterminals en tankbouw of tankomvorming;
* Ervaring met:

  + Marine infrastructuur zoals marine loading arms;
  + Ondergrondse of geboorde pijpleidingen;
  + Truck loading stations;
* Aantoonbare end-to-end projectervaring: van detailed engineering tot commissioning en opstart;
* Ervaring in samenwerking met EPC-contractoren (Engineering, Procurement & Construction);
* Kennis van of ervaring met COMAH/SEVESO-regelgeving.

**Persoonlijke kwaliteiten**

* Vloeiend in Nederlands en Engels;

* Productie- en resultaatgedreven;
* Actiegericht, besluitvaardig en hands-on ingesteld;
* Sterk in stakeholdermanagement en communicatie;
* Kan teams challengen op een constructieve manier;
* Gedijt goed in een ondernemende omgeving waarbij je zelf verantwoordelijkheid kan nemen.

#### **Ons aanbod**

* De kans om een strategisch internationaal conversieproject te realiseren in een dynamische industriële omgeving.
* Een sleutelrol met zichtbaarheid op directieniveau.
* De mogelijkheid om na afloop van het project mee te werken aan nieuwe projecten binnen de SEA-invest groep.
* Een langetermijnperspectief binnen een solide en internationaal actieve organisatie.

Indien u wordt uitgenodigd voor een gesprek, is het noodzakelijk om een recent uittreksel uit het strafregister aangaande havenarbeid te bezorgen. Dit uittreksel kan u aanvragen bij uw gemeente.

Heb je nog vragen over deze vacature? Neem dan gerust contact op met Veerle Bekaert op het nummer +32 3 560 25 12.

# Analyst, Private Equity Secondaries

London

We are global private markets specialists delivering tailored investment solutions, advisory services, and impactful, data driven insights to the world’s investors. Leveraging the power of our platform and our peerless intelligence across sectors, strategies, and geographies, we help identify the advantages and the answers our clients need to succeed.

The Analyst will be an integral part of StepStone's Private Equity Secondaries investment team, which recently closed its fifth fund with $7.4 billion of total capital commitments. StepStone deploys billions of dollars per year in private equity secondary deals, including GP-led transactions, LP interests in private equity funds and structured secondary deals (e.g., team spin-outs, direct investments, fund recapitalizations and other special situations).

StepStone prides itself on the firm’s collegial atmosphere, encouraging team-building initiatives and a collaborative approach. The position will have exposure to all levels of the firm globally, from Partners to fellow Analysts, on a daily basis.

**Position Overview:**

Your main responsibility will be to contribute to all aspects of the secondary deal process, including:

* Sourcing, screening and conducting due diligence on European private equity secondary investments (both LP and GP-led transactions);
* Interact with management teams and fund managers to conduct in-depth asset and portfolio-level analysis;
* Perform quantitative and qualitative research and financial modelling/analysis on companies and assets across stages,  industries and geographies;
* Preparation and presentation of due diligence materials and investment committee memos;
* Construct an opinion around various investment opportunities and efficiently communicate both verbally and in written materials; with the ability to defend your position in a team environment, including investment committee meetings;
* Support negotiation/coordination of deal closing/structuring process and post-close monitoring of existing investments; and
* Occasionally travel for onsite due diligence and to sponsor’s annual meetings to monitor investments.

**Requirements:**

* Stellar academic record (university and GPA);
* 1-2 years of private equity, top-tier investment banking and/or consulting experience;
* Excellent quantitative skills, including financial modelling, analytical and valuation skills for purpose of evaluating investment opportunities;
* Strong sense of risk/reward trade-offs, and an ability to display sound investment judgement;
* Strong appetite for self-directed learning, particularly in AI/automation, with demonstrated hands-on experimentation preferred;
* Self-starter, with strong ability to think creativity and conduct research to solve problems or find solutions;
* Ability to communicate and present ideas effectively, both verbally and in writing;
* Capable of multi-tasking with strong attention to detail;
* Promote and demonstrate a positive, team-oriented attitude, with desire to work on various projects; and
* Fluent (written and spoken) English; (additional language skills a plus).
